   "why": "Design 15 with Dm's pull on Q weakened (-8 -> -5), so the rhythm cannot latch on at night. In design 15's probes R2 stayed on all night: in darkness Dm reaches ~0.83, so Q's target while running was 8 - 6.6 = 1.4 (Q_out ~0.43), never past the 0.516 that ends a run (night beat 0.036). At -5 a night run drives Q toward 8 - 4.1 = 3.9 (Q_out ~0.9), so it ends; at rest Q's target at night is ~-3.8, so night rests stay short, as in design 14 (night beat ~0.01). In the far field (Dm ~0.26-0.38) the rest target is ~-0.9 to -1.5, so rests take ~0.5 tau (~50 ticks), about design 14's, and in bright light (Dm ~0.03) ~1.6 tau (~160 ticks, against design 14's ~90), so bright exploring stays low. Everything else is design 15's (Q bias -1.7). Expected in probes: darkness running < 50% with beat ~0.01; steady light 2-8 running < 10% (beat ~0.10); light 0.03-0.05 running ~30-40%; falls at 0.05 < 15%. In the walk calculator: crossing from 6,000 R near design 14's 1.09 h."
